From: Reilly Jones <70544.1227@compuserve.com>
Date: 19 Oct 94 02:19:41 EDT
Subject: [#94-10-324] Argument by Analogy (Uploads)

Marvin Minsky wrote 10/18/94: <Well, aren't there two different fitness spaces
to consider.  In the upload-duplication, even without any alterations,  we're
talking about populations in memetic, rather than in genetic space.> and then at
the end, <Tricky, because this will especially favor meme-systems that have
adopted evolutionary success as a positive value.   Which would seem to be more
or less inevitable, because the ones that don't do this will tend to die out.>

I put these two portions together because the answer to the first part is that
no, there aren't two different fitness spaces.  This becomes self-apparent by
the time you get to the last part.  Fitness only refers to purpose.  Values
adhere around purpose.  Memes adhere around values and perceptual
categorizations, they live in subjective selves but originate in consensual
reality, when "we" share our values, perceptions, and concepts.  Genes,
originating through self-organization and natural selection, produce homeostatic
values adhering around the only two purposes that biology alone has invented,
survival and reproduction.  Once culture arose within consensual reality, our
purposes have been expanding in pace with technological development.  For each
new purpose invented, new values, new perceptions, new concepts, new memes
cluster in a fitness landscape.  What we are really dealing with is one single
complex fitness space, what I term "purpose space."  Survival and reproduction
are currently the "great attractors" of this complex space, with many lesser
purposes spreading outward in variously sized clusters moving away from these
two biggies.

I hypothesize that the ultimate size and structure of purpose space is
unbounded.  I do not command the math ability to attempt to formulate this
rigorously.  I believe that uploads (as artifacts or children) would explore
deeper regions of purpose space than humans will, at least for the near-term
future, tied as we are to this solar system.  I do not see how it matters one
whit whether the upload has adult memes or not, each upload will search this
complex fitness space in complex ways.  It is hard for me to believe that even
an exact copy of memories and values will not quickly recontextualize these to
fit the new material substrate, since I accept the theories of consciousness
that posit that the mind is subjectively embodied.  Such recontextualization may
well lead to new purposes separate from human concerns, and out with the old
memes, in with the new.

